    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess. but \"living in the present\" sounds like a coping mechanism just to keep from looking at the math. if the universe is literally hardcoded to move toward nothingness, then staying in a state of constant struggle just to witness it feels... heavy. it feels like a burden. if everything is eventually going to be stripped away and forgotten by physics, why is there such a huge emphasis on the \"duty\" to keep persisting? why do we have to keep fighting this battle against entropy if the outcome is already decided?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
